cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CLMSynth: A Synthetic Data Generator for Cluster and Label Matching Evaluation"
abstract: >-
  CLMSynth generates a label L(x) and attaches it to an existing set of cluster
  IDs c(x) (ground truth or algorithm output), with the relationship between L
  and c specified by a configuration file rather than measured afterwards.
  Unlike clustering benchmarks that implicitly equate clusters with classes, it
  treats cluster formation and class assignment as independent processes with
  configurable matching outcomes, supporting mathematically controlled agreement
  through recall targets, class balance, spatial placement, and a solved target
  metric (multiclass Gorodkin R_K, a closed-form single-pair Matthews phi, or
  the adjusted Rand index).
type: software

